Package: statacompat
Title: Reproduce Selected 'Stata' Expression and Missing-Value Semantics
Version: 1.0
Date: 2026-10-30
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Ari Purwanto Sarwo", family = "Prasojo",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "ari.prasojo18@gmail.com",
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4862-5523")
    )
Description: A lightweight compatibility layer for researchers translating
    'Stata' data-management code into R. Provides vectorised helpers that
    reproduce selected 'Stata' expression semantics where they differ from
    base R, most importantly "Stata's" rule that numeric missing values are
    larger than every number: relational comparisons, inlist(), inrange(),
    cond(), missing(), and the 'egen' row functions rowtotal(), rowmean(),
    rowmiss() and rownonmiss(). Only the ordinary missing value is fully
    supported; "Stata's" extended missing values are detected and rejected
    wherever they would change a result.
